 you want to get the maximum  benefits from your green tea and of  course the best taste try Japanese or  Chinese grocers they tend to carry  better green teas and of course your  health stores to go for powdered or  loose leaf teas for maximum antioxidants  over tea bags loose leaf teas are made  from Holies bigger pieces of leaves and  tend to be fresher with short storage  life in contrast of a tea funning  teabags are usually made from small  pieces of tea leaves or tea Fanning's  which is quicker to brew but it lacks  the full flavor and health benefits they  tend to have a much longer storage life  which means they are not as fresh and  they will tend to lose lots of nutrients  but of course there will be some health  benefits as well so which Japanese or  Chinese green tea should you buy that I  would say really comes down to personal  taste and preference be open and keep  exploring the different kinds of green  teas and eventually you will find your  favorite when I stumble upon again my  child I was hooked and I've only been  drinking this ever since so explore and  let me know which is your favorite green  tea so now that you know more about  green tea why should you drink it every  day and what are some of the benefits  green tea contains a potent plant  nutrient also known as let me get this  right  epic gellar catechins galat or EGCG  4-shot EGCG has been studied to treat  various disease and is a natural  medicine the first benefit green tea is  a super fat fighter and helps towards  weight loss it's active ingredient EGCG  increases the rates of fat being burned  in our body we are recommended to drink  3 cups a day to increase our metabolic  rate however it is important to know  that green tea only increases our  metabolism by 4 percent which is about  80 calories a day so drinking green tea  alone will not help towards a  significant weight loss it is a  combination of regular exercises and  healthy eating  having said that green tea can help to  maintain a healthy weight and why not  burn some additional calories even  though it's a small amount because it  will help towards your weight loss in  long term you will be happy to know the  second benefit green tea targets  abdominal fat the EGCG in the green tea  activates fat burning genes in the  abdomen to speed weight loss by 77% so  drinking green tea on a daily basis will  help towards burning belly fat long-term  green tea helps to reduce bloating and  improves digestion it is a very powerful  diuretic which helps to relieve bloating  and avoid water retention so if you were  to drink green tea on a daily basis you  will notice that you will visit the  toilet more often to get rid of excess  water and toxic in your body which  actually helps towards a flat belly or  if you tend to experience feeling really  bloated after a meal try to drink a cup  of green tea which will help your body  to digest your food easily another  reason to drink green tea via 9 an amino  acid found in green tea can help with  relaxation and focus on a personal  experience I have to agree with this I  drink my green tea every morning either  before or with my breakfast and it  really helps to keep me calm and focus  right from the start of the day green  tea is also a great stress reliever so  whenever you get stressed out instead of  binging try to drink  cup of green tea to calm yourself down  or drink green tea whenever you're  studying or even working the fifth  reason it keeps our energy stable by  balancing our blood sugar levels this  will prevent blood sugar spikes or  crashes which can result in fatigue  irritability or cravings for unhealthy  food  green tea drinkers tend to be more in  control of their cravings and this can  also help towards binge eating so if  you're one of those person who is  constantly craving for more food even  when you are full try to drink green tea  every day and drink it with your meals  regular consumption of green tea also  help with longevity and looking young  EGCG is 200 times more powerful than  vitamin E to destroy skin damaging free  radicals  hence consuming green tea on a regular  basis were cute free radicals avoid skin  damaging wrinkles and other signs of  aging I genuinely believe that this is  one of the agent secret to youth boost  skin because we tend to consume green  tea on a daily basis you might not be  aware of this but green tea improves  dental health and reduces bad breath  unlike coffee which gives you bad breath  green tea does the total opposite the  anti bacterial and natural fluoride  found in green tea kills bacteria which  causes cavity tooth decay gum diseases  and bad breath so if you have a busy day  ahead you might want to consider  swapping your coffee with green tea this  powerful drink may also lower your risk  of cancer cancer is caused by  uncontrolled growth of cells and it is  one of the world's leading causes of  death EGCG is known to prevent lung  blarin stomach esophageal and breast  cancer by suppressing cancer growing  cells it has also been said that  drinking green tea before and after  so surgery significantly lowers the risk  of its reoccurrence so let's start  drinking green tea because prevention is  better than cure another health benefit  is green tea reduces bad cholesterol in  the blood and increases the good  cholesterol so this will help prevent  cardiovascular disease which is  currently the number one cause of deaths  in America so now that you know the  benefits of green tea how many cups  should you drink a day to gain the  maximum benefits there has been lots of  conflicting opinions on this sunset as  little as two cups some five cups and  some even up to 10 cups  I drink about 4 to 5 cups a day and I  would say that is a safe amount yes  green tea does contain caffeine but it  is much lower in comparison to coffee  one cup of green tea has about 35  milligram of caffeine whereas coffee has  between 100 to 200 milligrams of  caffeine  so the first infusion of green tea  releases the most caffeine and it starts  to reduce with a second and third  infusion if you are someone who is  sensitive to its cafe your limit should  only be one cup a day and try to go for  the third or second infusion so how to  make your green tea to get the maximum  flavor the first step is to bring a pot  of water to boil and allow it to stand  for two to three minutes because we do  not want the water to be boiling hot add  one or two teaspoons of tea leaves into  a tea pot pour the heated water and  allow the tea leaves to steam for up to  three minutes and enjoy your glass of  green tea if you were to steep the green  tea for more than three minutes it can  be rather bitter than flavorful you can  enjoy it hot or cool you can add a  little bit of flavor if you want to like  a squeeze of lemon or even ginger  whatever you do do not add milk to your  green tea the casing in the milk  inhibits the benefits of  see plus it is just weird and you will  not be able to gather maximum benefits  if you were to add sugar or artificial  sweeteners green tea on its own it's so  flavorful and so healthy in fact it is  zero in calories so why add all the  extras it is just not needed so to  conclude green tea is not something you  would start drinking for a couple of  months and then stop to gain the maximum  health benefits long-term drinking on a  regular basis every day I would only  drink water or green tea and without  fill I will have my green tea every  morning when I'm at home I will have  holies and when I'm traveling I would  carry the teabags with me of course they  may not be as fresh but it is my daily  devotion to green tea for new fitness  food and motivational videos please like  share and subscribe to my You Tube  channel and website do you follow me on  Facebook Instagram and Twitter to stay  connected with me thanks guys  you
 

